From: 3on3NHL-recomp
Subject: [PATCH] Don't stall the command processor after every resolve readback

With readback_resolve = full, every resolve waited for the GPU to finish all
submitted work before copying the result to guest memory - 10 to 17 times a
frame in this game, each time leaving the GPU idle while the command processor
recorded the next part of the frame, and the command processor idle while the
GPU caught up.

The guest GPU writes resolve results, fences and interrupts when it gets to
them, not when the command processor reads the packets. Do the same
(readback_resolve_deferred, on by default): copy each resolve result to a ring
of readback memory and submit, then write it to guest memory when its
submission has completed - polled between packets and while idle - together with
the fences (MEM_WRITE, EVENT_WRITE_SHD, scratch registers) and interrupts queued
behind it, in order. The command processor waits for the GPU only where the
command stream itself needs a queued value: WAIT_REG_MEM on a value not yet
written (it peeks at queued fences first, since a fence written earlier in the
stream precedes later commands on the guest GPU), and packets that read
registers or memory queued writes may change.

